{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeGenericSemisimple","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeGenericSemisimple","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TraceFormSemisimple","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerFactorial"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.isSemisimpleRing_of_one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.isSemisimpleRing_of_one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeGenericSemisimple.lean#L46-L56","doc":"**The substrate specialisation (sorry-free).**  For the real\nsubstrate `q > 1`, genericity is automatic (`qGeneric_of_one_lt`),\nso — modulo the same Gram–factorial identity — `A` is semisimple at\nevery rank.  This is the shape in which the substrate discharges the\nsemisimplicity leg of the `P ≠ NP`-in-QOU counting argument. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.isSemisimpleRing_of_qGeneric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.isSemisimpleRing_of_qGeneric","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeGenericSemisimple.lean#L33-L44","doc":"**Genericity ⇒ semisimple, modulo the Gram–factorial identity\n(sorry-free).**  Composes B1 (`qFactorial_ne_zero_iff`) with the\nabstract keystone B3d (`isSemisimpleRing_of_regTraceForm_nondegenerate`).\nThe hypothesis `hgram` is the Schur-element / Gram-determinant\ncontent that a concrete `H_n(q)` supplies; given it, a Wenzl-generic\nparameter makes the algebra semisimple. ","signatureChunk":0}]}